# proptest auto-saves a regression file next to a failing test; we
# don't pin past failures into version control. Two distinct shapes: some
# proptest versions/configs write a single *file* per crate whose name
# ends `.proptest-regressions`; the default (hit by Task 7's #567
# proptest, the first one under core/src) writes a *directory* literally
# named `proptest-regressions` at the crate root, mirroring the module
# path (e.g. `core/proptest-regressions/vault/canonical/value.txt` — this
# example path was verified by execution, deliberately breaking that
# proptest's comparator and observing where it wrote). The suffix-only
# pattern below does not match that directory form at all.
#
# #577: one exception. `len_then_bytes_matches_full_cbor_encoding_order`
# guards CanonicalMap::serialize's (byte length, bytes) key comparator
# against RFC 8949 §4.2.1. That is a FORMAT-FREEZING property — if it
# breaks, the on-disk layout of every record, block and manifest moves
# silently — and it is the property with the thinnest frozen-anchor
# coverage: mutating the comparator to chars().count() leaves
# golden_vault_001/002, conformance_kat and revoke_kat all green, because
# every key in those fixtures is ASCII (#562). A counterexample here is
# worth committing; the general policy above is unchanged.
#
# Git rule this depends on: a negation cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is itself excluded. The directory pattern used to be
# the bare `**/proptest-regressions/`, which excludes the directory node
# itself, so a plain `!core/proptest-regressions/vault/canonical/
# value.txt` negation against it did nothing (verified by execution).
# `**/proptest-regressions/**` below excludes the directory's *contents*
# instead, leaving the directory node itself un-excluded so git still
# descends into it — and the negations below re-include the one target
# file plus its two ancestor directories (each intermediate directory
# needs its own negation, or git never looks past it to the next).
**/*.proptest-regressions
**/proptest-regressions/**
!core/proptest-regressions/vault/
!core/proptest-regressions/vault/canonical/
!core/proptest-regressions/vault/canonical/value.txt

# uniffi-generated foreign-language bindings + compiled smoke runners.
# Bindings are regenerated by `tests/swift/run.sh` and `tests/kotlin/run.sh`
# on every invocation, so committing them would just create drift. The
# smoke-runner binaries (Swift native + Kotlin fat-jar) are build
# products of swiftc / kotlinc, not source. The Kotlin lib/ directory
# holds a fetched-and-verified jna.jar (integrity-pinned in run.sh).
/ffi/secretary-ffi-uniffi/bindings/
/ffi/secretary-ffi-uniffi/tests/swift/secretary_smoke
/ffi/secretary-ffi-uniffi/tests/swift/secretary_smoke.dSYM/
/ffi/secretary-ffi-uniffi/tests/swift/secretary_conformance
/ffi/secretary-ffi-uniffi/tests/swift/secretary_conformance.dSYM/
/ffi/secretary-ffi-uniffi/tests/kotlin/lib/
/ffi/secretary-ffi-uniffi/tests/kotlin/secretary_smoke.jar
/ffi/secretary-ffi-uniffi/tests/kotlin/secretary_conformance.jar

# Claude Code per-user state (settings, generated skills). Project-level
# Claude config (.claude/CLAUDE.md, .claude/agents/, etc.) may be
# committed selectively if introduced later.
# .claude/settings.local.json
# .claude/skills/

# Git worktrees — isolated per-feature branches live under .worktrees/
# (skill: superpowers:using-git-worktrees). Each worktree is its own
# branch checkout; the directory should not appear in main's tree.
.worktrees/

# Playwright MCP cache — local browser automation state, not source.
.playwright-mcp/

# Monitor smoke-test screenshots — eyeballed during NiceGUI dashboard
# verification, not artefacts worth committing. Scoped to repo root so
# committed asset PNGs (e.g. assets/secretary_logo.png) are unaffected.
/monitor-*.png

# Superpowers visual-companion (brainstorming UI) session state. Local
# scratch — mockups, server PIDs, and event logs that exist only for
# the duration of a brainstorming session.
.superpowers/

# `scripts/payload_guard/selftest.py`'s BP57 (#500 fix round 2, extended by
# #515) writes these files transiently to prove `run_real_scan`'s OWN
# production wiring is live — one probe per severable TERM, since no probe
# catches another's shape — then deletes them in a `finally` block, the
# PRIMARY guarantee against residue. These entries are belt-and-suspenders
# only, in case that block is ever interrupted (e.g. SIGKILL) before it runs.
/ffi/secretary-ffi-bridge/src/error/__selftest_shadow_wiring_probe.rs
/ffi/secretary-ffi-uniffi/src/__selftest_alias_wiring_probe.rs
/ffi/secretary-ffi-bridge/src/error/__selftest_gated_string_probe.rs
/ffi/secretary-ffi-bridge/src/error/__selftest_e6_wiring_probe.rs

